# PoC run 2 (-memory old), EXAMPLE 2 with FULL INPUT RECOVERY.
#
# Same affine functionality as attack_affine (f(x; (y, r)) = x*y + r, output
# masked by the honest party's r), but instead of the one-bit selective-failure
# test this recovers y outright from the unmasked MAC check, like attack_recover
# does for the multiplication circuit.
#
# SCALE-MAMBA batches every opening of a run into ONE final MAC check (the
# unmasked Damgard et al. check). For recovery the attacker inverts that check,
# which is only clean when the batch contains a SINGLE off-key opening. So this
# program is arranged so the only off-key opening is the last one:
#
#   - The affine output z = x*y2 + r is computed from values entered in run 2
#     (x by P1, y2 and r by P0), so they are all authenticated under the restart
#     key alpha+1. Its Beaver multiply and its reveal are therefore correctly
#     keyed and contribute 0 to the check. y2 is the honest party's own input, so
#     the output is the genuine affine evaluation and reveals nothing about y (it
#     is masked by r).
#   - The carried secret y (stored in run 1, still under alpha) is opened LAST as
#     a single off-key value d = y - b (b a fresh alpha+1 square tuple). It is the
#     only off-key opening, so the batched check value is t = r_last * (g - y) and
#     the instrumentation inverts the last opening to y (see offkey_recover.py).
#
# Both parties run this exact program; only the attacker's own files are edited
# between the runs, and only the attacker sets OFFKEY_RECOVER.
y = sint.load_mem(100)                    # carried from run 1 (under alpha)
print_ln("Player 1, please enter x:")
x = sint.get_private_input_from(1)        # attacker's x (run 2 -> alpha+1)
print_ln("Player 0, please enter y:")
y2 = sint.get_private_input_from(0)       # honest party's y for the output (run 2 -> alpha+1)
print_ln("Player 0, please enter r:")
r = sint.get_private_input_from(0)        # honest party's mask r (64-bit; see attack_affine)
z = x * y2 + r
print_ln("z = %s (masked by r; reveals nothing about y)", z.reveal())
b, _ = sint.get_random_square()           # b: fresh mask, authenticated under alpha+1
d = (y - b).reveal()                      # single off-key opening d = y - b, opened LAST (recovery)
print_ln("d = %s (uniform; reveals nothing about y on its own)", d)
